      "html": "<h5><svg class=\"md-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"1.15em\" height=\"1.15em\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"vertical-align:-0.2em;flex-shrink:0\"><path d=\"M21 5c-1.11-.35-2.33-.5-3.5-.5-1.95 0-4.05.4-5.5 1.5-1.45-1.1-3.55-1.5-5.5-1.5S2.45 4.9 1 6v14.65c0 .25.25.5.5.5.1 0 .15-.05.25-.05C3.1 20.45 5.05 20 6.5 20c1.95 0 4.05.4 5.5 1.5 1.35-.85 3.8-1.5 5.5-1.5 1.65 0 3.35.3 4.75 1.05.1.05.15.05.25.05.25 0 .5-.25.5-.5V6c-.6-.45-1.25-.75-2-1m0 13.5c-1.1-.35-2.3-.5-3.5-.5-1.7 0-4.15.65-5.5 1.5V8c1.35-.85 3.8-1.5 5.5-1.5 1.2 0 2.4.15 3.5.5z\"></path><path d=\"M17.5 10.5c.88 0 1.73.09 2.5.26V9.24c-.79-.15-1.64-.24-2.5-.24-1.7 0-3.24.29-4.5.83v1.66c1.13-.64 2.7-.99 4.5-.99M13 12.49v1.66c1.13-.64 2.7-.99 4.5-.99.88 0 1.73.09 2.5.26V11.9c-.79-.15-1.64-.24-2.5-.24-1.7 0-3.24.3-4.5.83m4.5 1.84c-1.7 0-3.24.29-4.5.83v1.66c1.13-.64 2.7-.99 4.5-.99.88 0 1.73.09 2.5.26v-1.52c-.79-.16-1.64-.24-2.5-.24\"></path></svg> References</h5>\n<p><svg class=\"md-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"1.15em\" height=\"1.15em\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"vertical-align:-0.2em;flex-shrink:0\"><path d=\"M8 16h8v2H8zm0-4h8v2H8zm6-10H6c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v16c0 1.1.89 2 1.99 2H18c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V8zm4 18H6V4h7v5h5z\"></path></svg> <a href=\"https://pythonspeed.com/articles/multi-stage-docker-python/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">pythonspeed: multi-stage builds for Python</a> · <svg class=\"md-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"1.15em\" height=\"1.15em\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"vertical-align:-0.2em;flex-shrink:0\"><path d=\"M8 16h8v2H8zm0-4h8v2H8zm6-10H6c-1.1 0-2 .9-2 2v16c0 1.1.89 2 1.99 2H18c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V8zm4 18H6V4h7v5h5z\"></path></svg> <a href=\"https://pythonspeed.com/articles/smaller-python-docker-images/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">pythonspeed: smaller Python Docker images</a></p>\n<h3 id=\"tldr\"><svg class=\"md-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"1.15em\" height=\"1.15em\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"vertical-align:-0.2em;flex-shrink:0\"><path d=\"M11 21h-1l1-7H7.5c-.88 0-.33-.75-.31-.78C8.48 10.94 10.42 7.54 13.01 3h1l-1 7h3.51c.4 0 .62.19.4.66C12.97 17.55 11 21 11 21\"></path></svg> TL;DR</h3>\n<p>Slim base, multi-stage build (compile in a builder, ship only installed packages), dependencies copied <em>before</em> app code, non-root user.\nLayers cache in order: put code first and every one-line edit reinstalls every dependency.</p>\n<h3 id=\"recall\"><svg class=\"md-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"1.15em\" height=\"1.15em\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"vertical-align:-0.2em;flex-shrink:0\"><path d=\"m19.07 4.93-1.41 1.41C19.1 7.79 20 9.79 20 12c0 4.42-3.58 8-8 8s-8-3.58-8-8c0-4.08 3.05-7.44 7-7.93v2.02C8.16 6.57 6 9.03 6 12c0 3.31 2.69 6 6 6s6-2.69 6-6c0-1.66-.67-3.16-1.76-4.24l-1.41 1.41C15.55 9.9 16 10.9 16 12c0 2.21-1.79 4-4 4s-4-1.79-4-4c0-1.86 1.28-3.41 3-3.86v2.14c-.6.35-1 .98-1 1.72 0 1.1.9 2 2 2s2-.9 2-2c0-.74-.4-1.38-1-1.72V2h-1C6.48 2 2 6.48 2 12s4.48 10 10 10 10-4.48 10-10c0-2.76-1.12-5.26-2.93-7.07\"></path></svg> Recall</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Prompt</th>\n<th>Answer</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>What does a multi-stage build buy?</strong></td>\n<td>Compilers and build caches stay in the builder; the final image ships only runtime files: smaller, less attack surface.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>The layer-caching rule?</strong></td>\n<td>Copy the dependency manifest and install <em>before</em> copying app code.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Two hygiene defaults?</strong></td>\n<td>A non-root <code>USER</code>, and a <code>.dockerignore</code> keeping <code>.git</code>, <code>.venv</code> and secrets out of the build context.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h3 id=\"the-idea\"><svg class=\"md-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"1.15em\" height=\"1.15em\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"vertical-align:-0.2em;flex-shrink:0\"><path d=\"M9 21c0 .55.45 1 1 1h4c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-1H9zm3-19C8.14 2 5 5.14 5 9c0 2.38 1.19 4.47 3 5.74V17c0 .55.45 1 1 1h6c.55 0 1-.45 1-1v-2.26c1.81-1.27 3-3.36 3-5.74 0-3.86-3.14-7-7-7m2.85 11.1-.85.6V16h-4v-2.3l-.85-.6C7.8 12.16 7 10.63 7 9c0-2.76 2.24-5 5-5s5 2.24 5 5c0 1.63-.8 3.16-2.15 4.1\"></path></svg> The idea</h3>\n<p>Use <code>python:3.12-slim</code>, not Alpine, whose musl libc forces slow source builds of many wheels. Layers cache in order: after editing <code>main.py</code>, the rebuild showed the <code>pip install</code> layer <code>CACHED</code>. Two traps hide in common snippets: Dockerfiles don't allow trailing <code>#</code> comments, so <code>COPY requirements.txt .   # deps first</code> failed to parse, and <code>chown -R app /app</code> is pointless without <code>WORKDIR /app</code>. With uv, install with <code>uv sync --frozen --no-dev</code> from the <a href=\"/python/virtual-environments-dependency-resolution\">lockfile</a>.</p>\n<h3 id=\"code\"><svg class=\"md-icon\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"1.15em\" height=\"1.15em\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"vertical-align:-0.2em;flex-shrink:0\"><path d=\"M9.4 16.6 4.8 12l4.6-4.6L8 6l-6 6 6 6zm5.2 0 4.6-4.6-4.6-4.6L16 6l6 6-6 6z\"></path></svg> Code</h3>\n<pre><code class=\"language-dockerfile\">FROM python:3.12-slim AS build\nWORKDIR /src\n# dependencies FIRST: this layer stays cached across code edits\nCOPY requirements.txt .\nRUN pip install --no-cache-dir --prefix=/install -r requirements.txt\n\n# clean runtime stage: no compilers or build caches shipped\nFROM python:3.12-slim\nCOPY --from=build /install /usr/local\nRUN useradd --create-home app\nWORKDIR /app\n# app code LAST: editing it doesn't reinstall dependencies\nCOPY --chown=app:app . .\nUSER app\nCMD [\"python\", \"main.py\"]\n</code></pre>"
    }
  ]
}
